{{- /*
error.gohtml is the panel's human-readable error page.

It does NOT replace the framework's JSON error envelope; it stands beside it. An
API endpoint writing an error still goes through the single gate and its body is
JSON. This page is only for paths inside the panel's own tree, the ones a
browser navigates to directly — showing JSON to a browser would make the error
unreadable.

The status code is chosen by the CALLER, not by the page: the same page serves
403 and 404, and the HTML writer carries the right code.
*/ -}}
{{ define "body" }}
<h1>{{ .Title }}</h1>
<p>{{ .Message }}</p>
{{ end }}
